WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.601 --> 00:00:03.501
-I'm so happy you're here.
I'm a big fans of both of you.

00:00:03.501 --> 00:00:04.534
Thank you so much
for being here.

00:00:04.534 --> 00:00:05.634
-Thank you.
-Congrats.

00:00:05.634 --> 00:00:07.300
"Ginny and Georgia,"
which, by the way,

00:00:07.300 --> 00:00:10.200
I think I was the first person
to watch the show.

00:00:10.200 --> 00:00:11.200
-Absolutely. I heard that.
-Of course. Yeah.

00:00:11.200 --> 00:00:13.100
-Thank you. I was, right?

00:00:13.100 --> 00:00:14.467
And I came in,
and everyone was like, "Oh, no.

00:00:14.467 --> 00:00:16.100
We're all watching it.
Everyone is obsessed."

00:00:16.100 --> 00:00:19.701
When Season 2 came out, it's the
number-1 show in 60 countries.

00:00:19.701 --> 00:00:21.400
Number 1.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:23.033 --> 00:00:25.300
Congratulations on that.

00:00:25.300 --> 00:00:27.400
Brianne, was there
a moment that you realized

00:00:27.400 --> 00:00:29.300
that the show was taking off?

00:00:29.300 --> 00:00:32.634
-Yeah. You know,
I was in Berlin over the summer.

00:00:32.634 --> 00:00:34.167
A very, very delayed honeymoon.

00:00:34.167 --> 00:00:38.167
And there happened to be
a marathon going by our hotel,

00:00:38.167 --> 00:00:40.834
so my husband and I are
standing, watching the marathon.

00:00:40.834 --> 00:00:44.467
And this very kind, grown man
runs out of the marathon

00:00:44.467 --> 00:00:48.267
and approaches us and tells me
how much he enjoys the show.

00:00:48.267 --> 00:00:50.334
And he says, "I know I'm not
your demographic,

00:00:50.334 --> 00:00:51.701
but I love the show."

00:00:51.701 --> 00:00:53.601
-He said, "I know
I'm not your demographic"?

00:00:53.601 --> 00:00:54.634
-Yeah.

00:00:54.634 --> 00:00:56.667
-That's funny
that he'd even say that.

00:00:56.667 --> 00:00:58.067
How about you, Antonia?

00:00:58.067 --> 00:01:01.167
When was the first time
you realized this show was big?

00:01:01.167 --> 00:01:05.167
-Yeah, I was just in Paris
recently for Fashion Week,

00:01:05.167 --> 00:01:08.300
and I was going up to my hotel,
and there was

00:01:08.300 --> 00:01:10.367
a group of people just
waiting outside.

00:01:10.367 --> 00:01:12.434
And I was like, "Oh, okay.
That's cool."

00:01:12.434 --> 00:01:15.501
And this one fan --
she came up to me

00:01:15.501 --> 00:01:17.300
and she was crying
and, like, shaking.

00:01:17.300 --> 00:01:18.834
And I didn't speak French,

00:01:18.834 --> 00:01:20.801
so I didn't know
how to properly comfort her.

00:01:20.801 --> 00:01:23.267
So, I just -- I gave her a big
hug, and she gave me a letter.

00:01:23.267 --> 00:01:25.734
And I went back to
my hotel room and I read it,

00:01:25.734 --> 00:01:27.234
and it was one of
the most heartfelt things

00:01:27.234 --> 00:01:29.467
I had read, I mean, just that
the show touched her so much.

00:01:29.467 --> 00:01:31.968
-A global -- It's a global hit.
-Yeah.

00:01:31.968 --> 00:01:33.067
-But I heard around the city,

00:01:33.067 --> 00:01:34.734
you have new rules
for walking around.

00:01:34.734 --> 00:01:37.100
-Yeah, because I live in
New York.

00:01:37.100 --> 00:01:38.834
-Yeah.
-And...

00:01:38.834 --> 00:01:42.067
[ Cheers and applause ]
Yeah, thank you. Thank you.

00:01:42.067 --> 00:01:44.234
And I've learned not to
leave my apartment

00:01:44.234 --> 00:01:46.467
at 3:00 p.m. on a weekday,
because then

00:01:46.467 --> 00:01:48.501
the high schoolers -- that's
when they get out of school.

00:01:48.501 --> 00:01:50.234
-That's your --
That is your demographic.

00:01:50.234 --> 00:01:51.868
-Yeah, that is my demographic.
-You will be mobbed.

00:01:51.868 --> 00:01:53.000
-And many of them are
bigger than me.

00:01:53.000 --> 00:01:54.133
-I don't know, though.

00:01:54.133 --> 00:01:55.267
Hey, it can be all times
of the day.

00:01:55.267 --> 00:01:56.534
-They're scary.
-Yeah, you're right.

00:01:56.534 --> 00:01:57.968
Now it's everybody.
-I love them, but they're scary.

00:01:57.968 --> 00:01:59.634
-I'm loving it too, yeah.

00:01:59.634 --> 00:02:02.100
Brianne, you went to school
here at NYU?

00:02:02.100 --> 00:02:03.534
-I did, yeah.
-That's wild.

00:02:03.534 --> 00:02:05.300
-I did.
-This is great.

00:02:05.300 --> 00:02:07.334
-I love New York.
-You love New York.

00:02:07.334 --> 00:02:09.067
-What do you love
about the city? Just...

00:02:09.067 --> 00:02:11.467
-It's spontaneous.
Anything can happen here.

00:02:11.467 --> 00:02:13.601
When I was a student at NYU,

00:02:13.601 --> 00:02:16.834
I was a receptionist at
a hair salon, actually.

00:02:16.834 --> 00:02:19.734
And I'm sitting there
at the front desk,

00:02:19.734 --> 00:02:22.267
and Hugh Jackman
and his two young kids

00:02:22.267 --> 00:02:23.501
go by on Razor scooters.

00:02:23.501 --> 00:02:25.801
And I -- It, like, made my day.

00:02:25.801 --> 00:02:27.534
But then, all of a sudden,
they circled back

00:02:27.534 --> 00:02:29.133
in the direction
they were coming from,

00:02:29.133 --> 00:02:30.901
and they come into the salon.

00:02:30.901 --> 00:02:33.033
And he asked, "Can my daughter
use the restroom?"

00:02:33.033 --> 00:02:36.634
And I think I just blacked out
and said, "Yes, absolutely."

00:02:36.634 --> 00:02:38.968
So, one of the women takes
the daughter to the restroom,

00:02:38.968 --> 00:02:41.367
and he and I are,
I think, making small talk.

00:02:41.367 --> 00:02:44.300
I tell him about NYU
and what I'm studying.

00:02:44.300 --> 00:02:46.267
And then, when his daughter
came back out,

00:02:46.267 --> 00:02:49.901
he said,
"Thank Brianne and say hi

00:02:49.901 --> 00:02:52.534
because she's gonna be
a famous actress one day."

00:02:52.534 --> 00:02:55.400
-Come on. Hugh Jackman.
How great is that guy?

00:02:55.400 --> 00:02:56.701
[ Cheers and applause ]
-Class act.

00:02:56.701 --> 00:03:01.100
-That's a class act.
-Yeah.

00:03:01.100 --> 00:03:03.300
-How did you find out
about this role?

00:03:03.300 --> 00:03:05.000
Did they come after you?
Did you audition for this?

00:03:05.000 --> 00:03:06.300
How did you know about this?

00:03:06.300 --> 00:03:09.234
-I was in the middle of
finals week at university.

00:03:09.234 --> 00:03:10.801
I was trying to graduate.
-Wow.

00:03:10.801 --> 00:03:13.033
-It was really difficult.
I barely did.

00:03:13.033 --> 00:03:16.200
And I get it in my in-box,
the audition.

00:03:16.200 --> 00:03:17.467
And I almost didn't
audition for it

00:03:17.467 --> 00:03:21.067
because I thought I was going to
fail out of school.

00:03:21.067 --> 00:03:23.434
But I read the script
and I really connected to

00:03:23.434 --> 00:03:26.100
the character in a way that
I hadn't before for other roles.

00:03:26.100 --> 00:03:28.534
And I knew that if I didn't
audition, I would regret it.

00:03:28.534 --> 00:03:29.767
So I did.

00:03:29.767 --> 00:03:31.601
And then like a couple weeks
after graduating,

00:03:31.601 --> 00:03:33.667
I was flying back and forth
six different times to L.A.

00:03:33.667 --> 00:03:34.868
to do chemistry reads.

00:03:34.868 --> 00:03:37.601
-So many times. This poor girl.
-Too many times.

00:03:37.601 --> 00:03:39.834
And, yeah,
I clearly do not regret it.

00:03:39.834 --> 00:03:42.701
It was such a crazy timeline.

00:03:42.701 --> 00:03:43.901
I was extremely lucky.
-Life-changing.

00:03:43.901 --> 00:03:45.400
-Yeah.
-Life-changing.

00:03:45.400 --> 00:03:48.100
And now you guys are -- Well,
you're "Ginny and Georgia" now.

00:03:48.100 --> 00:03:49.267
So this is all
that's happening now.

00:03:49.267 --> 00:03:50.934
-Yeah.
-"Ginny and Georgia."

00:03:50.934 --> 00:03:52.067
-That's it. Congrats.

00:03:52.067 --> 00:03:53.701
I think that's -- Now -- Yeah.

00:03:53.701 --> 00:03:56.601
But why do you think
the show's resonated with

00:03:56.601 --> 00:04:00.501
so many people
and different demographics?

00:04:00.501 --> 00:04:01.601
-I think there's
really just something

00:04:01.601 --> 00:04:02.634
for everyone in the show.

00:04:02.634 --> 00:04:03.868
-Mm-hmm.

00:04:03.868 --> 00:04:05.300
-You know, it's really,
like, hurried and fun,

00:04:05.300 --> 00:04:06.801
but it's also very real.

00:04:06.801 --> 00:04:08.167
We have such a diverse group
of characters

00:04:08.167 --> 00:04:09.300
with different experiences.

00:04:09.300 --> 00:04:10.834
-Story lines.
-Yeah.

00:04:10.834 --> 00:04:12.167
And I think --
-It touches so many subjects.

00:04:12.167 --> 00:04:13.534
-Yeah.
-And it's incredibly authentic.

00:04:13.534 --> 00:04:15.000
-Right.
-Yeah.

00:04:15.000 --> 00:04:17.834
-There's character for everyone
to really latch on to, so...

00:04:17.834 --> 00:04:19.734
-How do we set it up for
anyone who hasn't seen

00:04:19.734 --> 00:04:21.200
"Ginny and Georgia"?

00:04:21.200 --> 00:04:24.467
-Ooh! Season 2, we pick up
right where we left off.

00:04:24.467 --> 00:04:26.767
Only two weeks have passed.

00:04:26.767 --> 00:04:29.567
Ginny, unfortunately,
finds out that her stepfather

00:04:29.567 --> 00:04:31.834
did not die from natural causes

00:04:31.834 --> 00:04:34.000
and that her mother
actually murdered him

00:04:34.000 --> 00:04:36.200
on her behalf, so...

00:04:36.200 --> 00:04:38.334
There's just that elephant
in the room.

00:04:38.334 --> 00:04:39.601
-Yeah, that's -- Yeah.

00:04:39.601 --> 00:04:41.100
-But Georgia
is busy planning a wedding,

00:04:41.100 --> 00:04:42.300
so we're moving forward
and everything's fine.

00:04:42.300 --> 00:04:43.334
-Yeah, there are
more important things

00:04:43.334 --> 00:04:44.734
than to talk about murder.

00:04:44.734 --> 00:04:46.067
-Much more important things.
-Than you being a murderer.

00:04:46.067 --> 00:04:47.300
-Yeah.
-Yeah, of course.

00:04:47.300 --> 00:04:50.734
-Yeah, it's minor.
-But you're a young, single mom.

00:04:50.734 --> 00:04:52.267
I guess we can say that,
too, Georgia.

00:04:52.267 --> 00:04:54.234
So you guys play, yeah,
mother, daughter

00:04:54.234 --> 00:04:56.501
just before the murdering.

00:04:56.501 --> 00:04:57.801
-Well, and after.

00:04:57.801 --> 00:05:00.200
-If you haven't seen it,
I'm just setting that part up.

00:05:00.200 --> 00:05:02.100
-It's not a spoiler.
-No, it's not a spoiler, yeah.

00:05:02.100 --> 00:05:03.367
I want to show a clip.

00:05:03.367 --> 00:05:05.601
Here's Brianne Howey
and Antonia Gentry in

00:05:05.601 --> 00:05:06.667
"Ginny and Georgia."

00:05:06.667 --> 00:05:07.701
Take a look at this.

00:05:07.701 --> 00:05:10.834
♪♪

00:05:10.834 --> 00:05:12.200
-Mom.

00:05:12.200 --> 00:05:13.667
-Get out of here, Ginny.

00:05:13.667 --> 00:05:15.334
-What are you doing?
-I called Don.

00:05:15.334 --> 00:05:16.767
He told me about this book.

00:05:16.767 --> 00:05:18.601
He doesn't deserve to be
a teacher.

00:05:18.601 --> 00:05:21.801
-You don't think I know that?

00:05:21.801 --> 00:05:23.067
What happens if you're caught?

00:05:23.067 --> 00:05:24.567
You think they'll go easy on me?

00:05:24.567 --> 00:05:27.601
You can't just go around doing
whatever you want all the time.

00:05:27.601 --> 00:05:29.167
This is exactly why
I didn't tell you.

00:05:29.167 --> 00:05:31.968
You have no idea what things
are like for me sometimes.

00:05:31.968 --> 00:05:33.367
And I can't tell you anything,

00:05:33.367 --> 00:05:35.901
because then you might go and do
something insane like this.

00:05:35.901 --> 00:05:37.467
-I'm not going to sit back
and let someone

00:05:37.467 --> 00:05:38.667
treat my daughter this way.

00:05:38.667 --> 00:05:40.300
I'm your mother.

00:05:40.300 --> 00:05:43.434
No one on this Earth
loves you more than I do.

00:05:43.434 --> 00:05:44.534
-I know.

00:05:44.534 --> 00:05:48.868
-I would do anything
for you, okay?

00:05:48.868 --> 00:05:50.400
You know that.

00:05:51.767 --> 00:05:54.667
-Yeah. Come on.

00:05:54.667 --> 00:05:57.601
Brianne Howey, Antonia Gentry,
everyone!

00:05:57.601 --> 00:06:01.901
Season 2 of "Ginny and Georgia"
is streaming now on Netflix.

00:06:01.901 --> 00:06:03.434
We'll be right back with a
performance from

00:06:03.434 --> 00:06:04.934
Stephen Sanchez.

00:06:04.934 --> 00:06:06.467
Stick around, everybody.
Come on back.

